# case: 730-native-clients-run
# what: the Dockerfile layer that RESTORES the build toolchain never fires -- its
#       condition is changed to a value KEEP_BUILD_TOOLCHAIN can never hold, so
#       build-essential/libyaml-dev/zlib1g-dev/libssl-dev stay stripped even though
#       build.sh correctly passed KEEP_BUILD_TOOLCHAIN=1. This is the state that
#       shipped before that layer existed, and the reason it was added.
#
#       This targets the yaml.h assertion, NOT gcc. The first version of this
#       patch was written to target gcc and DID NOT DEMONSTRATE: run 31466356415
#       applied exactly this Dockerfile change and case 730 still passed all six
#       assertions. gcc survives the Dockerfile:219 `apt-get purge --auto-remove
#       build-essential` independently — build-essential is a metapackage and
#       --auto-remove keeps what other installed packages still need. So 730's
#       stated reason for asserting gcc ("if the Dockerfile ever stripped the
#       toolchain again despite the flag") was unfalsifiable, and a patch named
#       730-toolchain-stripped sitting beside it implied otherwise. 730 now also
#       asserts /usr/include/yaml.h, which libyaml-dev provides and which nothing
#       else in the Dockerfile installs — present if and only if this layer ran.
#
#       Mutating the Dockerfile rather than build.sh is deliberate. build.sh sets
#       KEEP_BUILD_TOOLCHAIN=1 whenever ruby, db-clients OR c-toolchain is set, and
#       the native variant sets the first two, so no build.sh edit can produce
#       KEEP_BUILD_TOOLCHAIN=0 there. Forcing the ARG to 0 directly is also not it:
#       the RUBY_RUNTIME layer fails
#       the build outright on RUBY_RUNTIME=1 with KEEP_BUILD_TOOLCHAIN!=1, so the
#       image would never build and 730 would fail as "image did not build" — a
#       named failure, but not this one. Defeating the restore layer while leaving
#       the flag truthful reproduces the actual defect: the flag says keep, the
#       image does not have it.
#
#       MUST BE DEMONSTRATED ALONE (--cases 730-native-clients-run). rvm needs
#       this layer's headers to build psych, so 740/750/760 would fail for this
#       mutation's reason before reaching their own assertions — the masking that
#       cost three extra dispatches last increment.
#
#       Expected: 730's yaml.h assertion FAILS ("libyaml-dev's header is
#       MISSING"), while all six binaries -- INCLUDING gcc, for the reason above
#       -- still PASS. A run where gcc also fails means something else changed.
#
diff --git a/Dockerfile b/Dockerfile
--- a/Dockerfile
+++ b/Dockerfile
@@ -291,7 +291,7 @@
 # interface, which is what lets `c-toolchain=ON` alone be sound without an image
 # variant built to prove it (backlog F60).
 ARG KEEP_BUILD_TOOLCHAIN=0
-RUN if [ "$KEEP_BUILD_TOOLCHAIN" = "1" ]; then \
+RUN if [ "$KEEP_BUILD_TOOLCHAIN" = "NEVER" ]; then \
       apt-get update && apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends \
         build-essential libyaml-dev zlib1g-dev libssl-dev && \
       rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*; \
